Package: robscale
Type: Package
Title: Robust Location and Scale Estimation with SIMD-Accelerated C++ Kernels
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Dennis Alexis Valin", family = "Dittrich",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "davd@economicscience.net",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4438-8276")))
Description: Provides high-performance C++ implementations of robust location
    and scale estimators. The M-estimators of Rousseeuw & Verboven (2002)
    <doi:10.1016/S0167-9473(02)00078-6> target very small samples (n <= 8)
    with SIMD-accelerated tanh iteration. The Rousseeuw-Croux Qn and Sn
    estimators (Rousseeuw & Croux, 1993) use cache-aware algorithm dispatch,
    Floyd-Rivest selection, and multi-threaded kernels (via RcppParallel) to
    scale from n=2 to n=10^8 with 2--14x speedup over robustbase.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/davdittrich/robscale,
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18828607
BugReports: https://github.com/davdittrich/robscale/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), RcppParallel (>= 5.0.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppParallel, BH
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), revss, microbenchmark
SystemRequirements: GNU make, TBB (Intel Threading Building Blocks), C++17
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
